<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Cyclone DDS config for running this demo *beside another SpatialDDS
  deployment on one host* — specifically OpenVPS's `spatialdds` AWS variant.

  Point the launcher at it:

      SPATIALDDS_DDS_DOMAIN=0 \
      SPATIALDDS_DDS_CONFIG=$PWD/deploy/aws/cyclonedds-colocated.xml \
      SPATIALDDS_MOCK_VPS=0 ./run_bridge_server_docker.sh

  It is mounted *at* /etc/cyclonedds.xml rather than named by CYCLONEDDS_URI,
  which `require_dds_env` refuses to let differ.

  **Why it is not the default, and why the default cannot be used there.**
  The repository's `cyclonedds.xml` leaves multicast on, which is correct
  everywhere this demo normally runs. An AWS VPC does not carry multicast, so
  OpenVPS's variant turns it off and discovers unicast against a peer list —
  and two participants that disagree about multicast on one host do not fail,
  they simply never find each other. Cyclone reports an absence of peers, not
  an error, so the visible symptom is an empty venue and a localize that never
  returns. That asymmetry is the whole reason this file exists.

  Deliberately a byte-for-byte match of the discovery half of
  `openvps-deploy/deploy/aws/cyclonedds.xml.in` (with no PEERS marker to
  render): the two sides have to agree, and the way to keep them agreeing is
  to copy rather than to re-derive. `ParticipantIndex=auto` probes the local
  port range, which is what makes an empty peer list right for a single host —
  both stacks on one instance is exactly that case.

  For two hosts, each side needs the other's private address as a Peer. That
  is the `DdsPeers` stack parameter on OpenVPS's side and would need the
  mirror here; not written until something needs it.
-->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config">
  <Domain id="any">
    <General>
      <Interfaces>
        <NetworkInterface autodetermine="true"/>
      </Interfaces>
      <AllowMulticast>false</AllowMulticast>
    </General>
    <Discovery>
      <ParticipantIndex>auto</ParticipantIndex>
      <Peers></Peers>
    </Discovery>
  </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
